@echo off
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE WHILE IT IS RUNNING. NOT EVEN A COMMENT.
rem
rem cmd.exe reads a batch file INCREMENTALLY, BY BYTE OFFSET, as it executes
rem it. Changing the file's length mid-run moves everything after the cursor,
rem and execution resumes at an offset that no longer means what it meant.
rem
rem That cost INFRA-VIEWER-001 a four-hour qualification that had PASSED: two
rem minutes in, a comment was reworded; four hours later, when qualify.cmd
rem returned, cmd.exe resumed at a stale offset and called it a SECOND time,
rem truncating qualification-times.txt and overwriting three of debug-ext's
rem logs. The run had already printed "every stage exited 0" and the evidence
rem for it was gone.
rem
rem EVERY LINE OF THIS FILE BEGINS WITH rem, set, call, echo, setlocal,
rem endlocal OR @echo FOLLOWED BY A SPACE OR THE END OF THE LINE, AND THAT IS
rem CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN BY A WHOLE-WORD MATCH. P19-ARCH-001's copy had a
rem line beginning "remrem" that a prefix match let through; cmd ran it as a
rem command and printed "not recognized" to stderr. P19-FLUID-001 fixed the
rem line and the check, and the check has caught the same splice twice since.
rem ---------------------------------------------------------------------
rem
rem P19-CONT-001 CONTINUITY EQUATION. The exact invocation, recorded so the run
rem is reproducible rather than described.
rem
rem qualify.cmd is byte-identical to the one P16-SIZE-001 settled on and every
rem milestone since has used, SIXTY-FOUR in a row counting this one. Every
rem file in this directory except THIS one is a byte-identical copy of
rem P19-MOM-001's, verified by hash before the run:
rem
rem   qualify.cmd          git hash-object d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b
rem   verify-harness.cmd   git hash-object 11855b8ff891093b021d1e0351761283d0eedd24
rem   launch.cmd           git hash-object f11039e6dc366d7c469a15cf74fb3867fd5ffeff
rem   preflight-space.cmd  git hash-object a65d6578000b6e8a2811d5154bcec24be09c2b54
rem   preflight-space.ps1  git hash-object 2f0d4228488f6a574ca57ec89f0fad0107b16b59
rem
rem AND THE REPEAT FILTER BELOW IS BYTE-IDENTICAL TO P19-MOM-001's TOO, so the
rem only difference between this qualification and that one is THE TREE UNDER
rem TEST. This milestone touches nothing below cfd -- it adds one header, one
rem source, one unit suite and one compile-fail group, and modifies three CMake
rem lists by one line each -- so the nine core math and units prefixes
rem P19-GEOM-001 added for its layer-0 header change are not required by this
rem blast radius. They are KEPT anyway. A determinism gate is not shrunk
rem because a milestone happens not to need it.
rem
rem WHAT THIS MILESTONE ADDS. cfd gains the continuity evaluation
rem (CfdContinuity.hpp and .cpp, ADR-074): an eight-phase gate, and a report
rem that CONSUMES the already-qualified divergence for the per-cell residuals
rem and the global sums while walking boundary faces only for the inlet/outlet
rem and per-patch attribution that operator cannot do, because it takes no
rem boundary. It computes the two mass-balance measures ADR-058 fixed and
rem CfdData.hpp already declares; it defines neither, sets no throughput floor
rem and judges nothing. It produces no field and performs no solve.
rem
rem NO HEADER BELOW cfd CHANGES, which is what makes the repeat set identical.
rem No existing source file is modified at all: the only edits outside the four
rem new files are one line in each of three CMake lists, plus TODO.md and
rem ROADMAP.md, which cannot change an executable. The subtree hashes recorded
rem by qualify.cmd cover all of them regardless.
rem
rem MEASURED AGAINST THE FROZEN TREE, so the logs can be read against a number
rem rather than for an absence of the word "fail". The three figures are in
rem FREEZE.md with their derivations, counted off the frozen tree by
rem `ctest -N` rather than predicted -- P19-GEOM-001's freeze recorded getting
rem that wrong once, and P19-CONV-001's recorded two of its own figures
rem mislabelled.
rem
rem compile_fail stays EXCLUDED from the repeat, as in every milestone (each
rem case is a real compilation, and the groups take minutes serialised on the
rem build-tree lock); the new compile_fail.cfdcont group's 37 cases run in the
rem full ctest of all three presets.
rem
rem QUALIFY_REPEAT is expanded as !REPEAT! inside qualify.cmd, never %REPEAT%:
rem a %VAR% holding | ( or ) is substituted when the for-block is PARSED and
rem closes the block early, killing the run after every preset has passed.
rem
rem THIS RUN HAPPENS ON THE HASIB MACHINE, as every milestone since P17-CLI-001,
rem by the owner's decision of 2026-10-14. GCC 16.1.0 WinLibs POSIX UCRT r4,
rem the CMake 4.4.1 and Ninja it bundles, and the dependency prefix built by
rem deps/CMakeLists.txt from the same hash-verified archives: Qt 6.11.2, OCCT
rem 8.0.1, zlib 1.3.1, Netgen 6.2.2604.
rem
rem THE RELEASE PRESET WAS BUILT TO COMPLETION, AND AFTER THE LAST EDIT, BEFORE
rem THIS FREEZE EXISTED. That ordering is P19-MOM-001's lesson and it is why
rem this file can be trusted at all: that milestone's first attempt failed 66m28s
rem in on a -Werror=array-bounds rejection at -O3 in a test helper, of a class
rem that had been found and fixed in a SIBLING helper before its freeze and
rem recorded as caught. A fix at one site is not a fix of a class, and a preset
rem built before the last edit has not been built. Both presets here were
rem rebuilt after the final edit and proved current by a no-op build rather
rem than by a timestamp.
rem
rem BEFORE LAUNCHING, the disk is checked. preflight-space.cmd measures the
rem %TEMP% volume and the build-root volume, refuses below
rem QUALIFY_MIN_FREE_GB, and ends the process rather than reaching the
rem qualify.cmd line below. The check is its own pair of files because a
rem comparison cannot live in THIS file: `if` is not one of the allowed line
rem prefixes, and qualify.cmd is byte-identical across sixty-three milestones
rem and is not this milestone's to touch.
rem
rem QUALIFY_MIN_FREE_GB stays at 20, the figure the owner chose on 2026-10-30
rem from a measurement recorded in P19-MESH-001's FREEZE.md.
rem
rem THE FRESHNESS HALF of the fresh-binary proof (the binaries are newer than
rem the clean and than the newest source) is done after the run, by hand, and
rem recorded in the evidence. P19-MOM-001's own freshness check had a defect in
rem its first form -- `dir /s /b /o-d` sorts within each path argument and not
rem across them, so it named a two-month-stale file as the newest under the
rem frozen surface -- so this one uses a single global sort.
setlocal
rem
rem TOOLCHAIN PINNING, 2026-10-30, replacement machine. A fresh process on
rem this machine resolves gcc and cmake to MSYS2 UCRT64 -- GCC 16.2.0 and
rem CMake 4.4.3 -- and NOT to the pinned WinLibs GCC 16.1.0 / CMake 4.4.1;
rem WinGet's PATH shim does not even satisfy `where gcc`. Without the line
rem below the harness would silently qualify the WRONG TOOLCHAIN, and no
rem later check would catch it, because every test count, warning count and
rem subtree hash would still look exactly right. The pinned bundle carries
rem gcc, g++, cmake, ctest and ninja together, so putting it first pins all
rem five in one line.
set "PATH=%LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\WinGet\Packages\BrechtSanders.WinLibs.POSIX.UCRT_Microsoft.Winget.Source_8wekyb3d8bbwe\mingw64\bin;%PATH%"
rem
rem TLS TRUST. That bundled CMake ships no CA bundle ("no trust anchors
rem configured"), so the Catch2 FetchContent download fails certificate
rem verification and the configure stage dies before anything is built. The
rem harness runs a bare `cmake --preset` and cannot be passed
rem -DCMAKE_TLS_CAINFO, but libcurl inside CMake reads these two. This adds
rem TRANSPORT trust only: TLS verification stays ON and every pinned archive
rem hash is still enforced, so nothing about content verification changes.
set "CURL_CA_BUNDLE=C:\Program Files\Git\mingw64\etc\ssl\certs\ca-bundle.crt"
set "SSL_CERT_FILE=C:\Program Files\Git\mingw64\etc\ssl\certs\ca-bundle.crt"
set "BETTERCAD_BUILD_ROOT=C:/bettercad/bc-build"
rem BUILD PARALLELISM. 4, carried from P19-CONV-001's second attempt, which is
rem where the number was measured. P19-CONV-001's attempt 1 at 16 lost a
rem compile with no diagnostic whatever and an orphaned 0-byte %TEMP%\cc*.s:
rem cc1plus died before writing any assembly, because the resource is COMMIT
rem rather than disk or RAM alone.
rem
rem     commit before any build        71.3 GB used of an 80.8 GB limit
rem     per debug compile job          1.81 GB
rem     wanted at 16                   about 29 GB, against about 9.5 GB free
rem     the test executable LINK       10.3 GB of commit for a 1.40 GB binary
rem
rem THE LINK IS A SINGLE PROCESS AND NEEDS ITS 10.3 GB AT ANY -j, so lowering
rem the bound controls the compile phase only. At 4 that phase peaks near
rem 78.5 GB and the link stays the one tight spot, measured to fit rather than
rem assumed to.
rem
rem WHAT THIS DOES NOT CHANGE. Build parallelism changes build time only:
rem ninja compiles the same sources with the same flags and -Werror at any -j,
rem and ctest's own -j 8 lives in qualify.cmd, which is not this milestone's to
rem touch and stays at d313a64070718c44fae290ac042fe259d1a03c8b. No preset, no
rem test, no filter and no source file is altered by it. This is a resource
rem parameter, NOT a gate.
set "CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=4"
set "QUALIFY_PRESETS=debug-ext release-ext debug-shared-ext"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT_PRESETS=release-ext debug-ext"
set "QUALIFY_MIN_FREE_GB=20"
set "QUALIFY_REPEAT=architecture|unit\.Linalg|unit\.Structural|unit\.Cfd|unit\.Fluid|unit\.Provenance|unit\.CustomMaterial|unit\.MaterialFile|unit\.MaterialCli|unit\.Thermal|unit\.P18Qualification|unit\.P17Qualification|unit\.Quality|unit\.MeshDofMap|unit\.ConstraintSet|unit\.FreeEquationMap|unit\.Tet4Element|unit\.Mesh|unit\.Volume|unit\.Tet|unit\.Siz|unit\.Id|unit\.ReferenceModel|unit\.Analytic|unit\.View|unit\.RigidTransform|unit\.Transform|unit\.Point|unit\.Direction|unit\.Frame|unit\.Unit|unit\.Dimension|unit\.MassProperties|unit\.SurfaceMesh|refmod\.|gui\.|cli\.thermal\.|cli\.structural\.|cli\.mesh\."
call "%~dp0preflight-space.cmd"
call "%~dp0qualify.cmd" "%~dp0."
set "RESULT=%errorlevel%"
echo qualify.cmd exit %RESULT%
endlocal & exit /b %RESULT%
